# Scripts stay local — they hold keys, one-off jobs and scraped data. The exceptions are the two
# that carry no secrets and exist to keep D1 agreeing with the rules in lib/: the lead sourcing CLI,
# lost twice with the sourcing rules inside it, and the area reclassifier, whose absence turns the
# next change to AREAS into a hand-written migration restating every ZIP range. Written as
# `scripts/*` rather than `scripts/`, because git does not descend into an excluded directory and
# a negation under one never matches.
scripts/*
!scripts/get-leads.ts
!scripts/reclassify-areas.ts
# Cuts the homepage photography from the masters in ph/ into the AVIF/WebP renditions under
# public/photos and prints lib/photos.ts. No keys, no scraped data, and without it the only way
# back to a rebuilt crop is by hand.
!scripts/build-photos.mjs
# The masters build-photos.mjs cuts those renditions from. ~40MB of JPGs that nothing at
# runtime reads, so they stay out of the repo and live alongside it instead.
ph/
docs/*
!docs/onboarding/
docs/onboarding/*
!docs/onboarding/README.md
# Living documentation: the Mermaid sources are meant to be reviewed alongside the code they draw.
# Everything else under docs/ (research, outreach CSVs, dated proposals) stays local.
!docs/diagrams/
# d1/ holds migrations and nothing else. Everything else written there is generator output —
# seeds, requeues, rescans — carrying real businesses' phone numbers and addresses, so the rule
# admits the migrations directory rather than naming each generated family and missing the next one.
d1/*
!d1/migrations/
# Working notes, internal specs, sales material — anything that stays off the remote
/local/
# Playwright MCP scratch output — page snapshots and screenshots taken while working.
.playwright-mcp/
